1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Calculator vs AI — why one of them can't multiply

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,200
Part 1 of 3: THE CALCULATOR

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,400
13 + 11

4
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,600
In binary, with logic gates: 1101 + 1011

5
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,400
It starts at the SMALLEST digit.  S = A XOR B XOR C

6
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,200
The carry ripples right to left, one column at a time

7
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,400
= 24

8
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,200
Every carry moves left. It has no choice.

9
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,800
Part 2 of 3: THE AI

10
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,000
A language model writes left to right — so it says the BIGGEST digit first

11
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
317 × 315 = 99,855        317 × 316 = 100,172

12
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,800
Change the LAST digit going in, and the FIRST digit coming out flips

13
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,800
GPT-4 multiplication accuracy: 3 digits 59%, 4 digits 4%, 5 digits 0%

14
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,600
Five digits: zero out of a hundred.  Source: Goat, arXiv:2305.14201

15
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,000
Part 3 of 3: SIDE BY SIDE

16
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,800
Calculator: smallest digit first.  AI: biggest digit first.

17
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:25,600
Calculator: logic gates.  AI: prediction.

18
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,400
Calculator: always exact.  AI: 0% at 5 digits.

19
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,800
Calculator: right by construction.  AI: right by resemblance.

20
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,200
One computes the answer. The other predicts it.

21
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:35,200
Pause. Observe. Learn.  Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
